WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.330
In 2000, China's reported trade with African
countries was worth about 10.6 billion

2
00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:07.090
dollars.

3
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:11.390
By 2010, it was about 127 billion.

4
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:17.050
By 2024, about 295 billion,
in current dollars.

5
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.770
Copper and oil flow one way.

6
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:22.330
Machinery and vehicles flow back.

7
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.810
So who gains most from the deal?

8
00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:25.990
Mostly China?

9
00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:27.780
Mostly African countries?

10
00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:31.110
In this mission, you'll trace
what is traded each way,

11
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:36.010
and the opportunities it opens for
African economies and for China.

12
00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:38.410
Then you'll weigh the
challenges each side faces,

13
00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:42.410
and judge who gains
more, and on what terms.

14
00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:46.990
Your mission: decide who gains most
from China's trade with Africa.
